-- title:
--   Surjectivity of Vélu maps over an algebraically closed field
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field and $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $K$ that is elliptic. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \neq 2$ and $\ell \neq 0$ in $K$, and let $Q$ be a point of the affine model `W.toAffine` whose additive order is exactly $\ell$. Put $S =$ `W.oddOrderSummingSet Q (ℓ / 2)`, the finite subset of $K \times K$ obtained as the image of $\{1,\dots,\lfloor \ell/2\rfloor\}$ under $k \mapsto$ the coordinate pair of $k \bullet Q$ (the point at infinity being sent to $(0,0)$). Let `W.veluQuotient S` be the Weierstrass curve with the same $a_1,a_2,a_3$ as $W$, with $a_4$ replaced by $a_4 - 5\sum_{P \in S} t(P)$ and $a_6$ by $a_6 - b_2\sum_{P \in S} t(P) - 7\sum_{P \in S} w(P)$, where $t$ is Vélu's `veluT` and $w$ is `veluW`. The assertion is that every additive group homomorphism $\varphi$ from the points of `W.toAffine` to the points of the affine model of `W.veluQuotient S` which, on every affine point $(x,y)$ with nonsingularity witness not lying in the subgroup of integer multiples of $Q$, takes the value given by Vélu's coordinate formulae `W.veluX S x` and `W.veluY S x y` (for some nonsingularity witness), is surjective.
--
--   This is the statement, for Vélu's explicit model of the quotient of $W$ by the cyclic group generated by a point of odd prime order, that a nonconstant isogeny over an algebraically closed field is surjective on points. It is used where a point of the quotient curve must be lifted along the Vélu map, in the construction of rational homomorphisms with prescribed kernel and in the analysis of fibres over a modular curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_veluPointHom_surjective_of_isAlgClosed.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassCurve_Velu
import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassCurve_VeluQuotientMap
import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassCurve_VeluPointMap
import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassCurve_OddOrderSummingSet

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open Polynomial WeierstrassCurve WeierstrassCurve.Affine

theorem WeierstrassCurve.veluPointHom_surjective_of_isAlgClosed
    {K : Type*} [Field K] [DecidableEq K] [IsAlgClosed K] (W : WeierstrassCurve K) [W.IsElliptic]
    {ℓ : ℕ} (hℓ : ℓ.Prime) (hℓ2 : ℓ ≠ 2) (hℓK : (ℓ : K) ≠ 0)
    (Q : W.toAffine.Point) (hQord : addOrderOf Q = ℓ) :
    let S := W.oddOrderSummingSet Q (ℓ / 2)
    ∀ φ : W.toAffine.Point →+ (W.veluQuotient S).toAffine.Point,
      (∀ (x y : K) (h : W.toAffine.Nonsingular x y),
        (.some x y h : W.toAffine.Point) ∉ AddSubgroup.zmultiples Q →
          ∃ h', φ (.some x y h) = .some (W.veluX S x) (W.veluY S x y) h') →
      Function.Surjective φ := by sorry
